{"id": "000VIX", "title": "The Grass is Greener...", "posted": "Gestern, 23:56 Uhr", "author": "sisaloofafump", "rules": "Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\nShaded cells: Shade 5 cells in every box except for one. The remaining box gets none. These shaded cells form an orthogonally connected area across the board. Within the shaded area, cells cannot have a difference greater than 2 from their neighbour. (For example, a shaded 5 can share an edge with a shaded 3, 4, 6, or 7. It cannot share an edge with a shaded 9.) They can share an edge with any unshaded cell.\n\nUnshaded cells: All unshaded cells that have a difference of 5 or more from their unshaded neighbours are marked with a green German Whispers line. They do not have to be orthogonally connected or form a continuous group. They can share an edge with any shaded cell.\n\nXVs: Digits separated by an X sum to 10. Digits separated by a V sum to 5. Exactly one of the cells in each marked pair is shaded.\n\nAnti-XVs Shading: If elsewhere in the grid there are cells that sum to 10 or 5 with their neighbour, both of the cells are either shaded or unshaded.\n\nIt aint the prettiest but i really love the solve path in this one. Hope you enjoy!\n\nPlay on SudokuPad", "solutionCode": "Row 5 with a \"/\" marking the shaded/unshaded borders. e.g. 12/34/567/8/9", "difficulty": 2, "solvedCount": 2, "tags": ["Sudoku", "German Whispers (Variante)", "X-Sums (Variante)"], "links": [{"url": "https://sudokupad.app/fnfizbsj7j", "kind": "sudokupad"}], "firstSeen": "2026-10-17T17:00:00+00:00", "data": "", "link": "https://sudokupad.app/fnfizbsj7j", "linkKind": "sudokupad", "settings": {}, "summary": {"format": "scl", "decoded": true, "rows": 9, "cols": 9, "cages": 0, "hasSolution": true, "features": ["lines", "overlays"]}}